  "instruction": "Claude r21 (2026-09-28): the game-script side of the menu-bar 「모드」 menu, stage 1 (design ingame/설계_v4_메뉴바차트.md 「B」 and 「프로토콜(확정, 09-28 02시)」; the native hook is a separate install). Codex must never run publish_calendar_*.py --restore or publish_modmenu_*.py --restore or otherwise remove the calendar overlay (KR_T9*/KR_T17*/KR_T18*/KR_T19*/KR_T20* functions, the nine r15 same-length operands, the RunEvent operand swap in KR_T9HomeCasual, the seven r20 same-length operands in C_Status::RunStatus, C_HomeStatusView@SetInfo, C_SceneTraining@RunSelectPartner and C_SceneTraining@_UpdateInputPartner) or the mod-menu request consumer (KR_M* functions and the two r21 same-length operands: KR_T9HomeMenuRun calls KR_MHomeRun where it called ■選択ダイアログ／実行, C_SelectDialog@_Update calls KR_MTick where it called C_UserInputManager::IsClickEnterOtherMouse). The calendar and the mod menu are permanent user-requested features: when a rebuild needs a clean base, rebase on the runtime that current.json points to and carry the calendar and mod-menu functions forward; restore is reserved for the user's explicit request. Payload: NightRemaster.ain only; PACT/EX/FNL, the help-menu chart and winmm.dll untouched. KR_M* functions appended; no original function relocated, no forwarder, no new global / struct member, no save schema change; two session variables YoruKR.M.Home (armed while the home menu waits) and YoruKR.M.Off (polling stopped for the session when a request file cannot be deleted). Two same-length CALLFUNC operand swaps: KR_T9HomeMenuRun ■選択ダイアログ／実行 -> KR_MHomeRun (arms the poll while the home menu of RunHome waits; when the wait ends with KR_MCode 2026092801 it serves the request after the menu closed and returns KR_T8HomePickCode so KR_T8HomeMenuClose loops and RunHome rebuilds its menu); C_SelectDialog@_Update C_UserInputManager::IsClickEnterOtherMouse -> KR_MTick (every frame of every selection dialog: only while armed it checks KRMenu\\request.txt and KRMenu\\last_result.txt and ends the wait with KR_MCode; otherwise it returns the original query). Files: <game folder>\\KRMenu\\request.txt (hook: cmd / seq / time, CR LF) read and deleted; unknown commands deleted and ignored; last_result.txt shown (first line, half-width set, wrapped at 38) and deleted; <save folder>\\YoruKR_Chart.dat 「YoruKR.Chart.1」 + 0/1 (TextFile, as the 09-24 terms file; KR_MUnlockAll reads it and is not connected to anything in stage 1); reset_all / reset_restore after an in-game 예: <save folder>\\YoruKR_reset.marker 「reset」 / 「restore」 (TextFile: plain bytes; VSFile would write a VSF header the hook does not read) then <game folder>\\KRMenu\\<word>.req, the opposite .req removed, then system.Exit(0) + system.Peek (the tail of Ａ＿ゲーム終了); the hook does backup / delete / restore at the next start. <runtime>/KRMenu/ is the temporary exchange-file folder of the mod-menu hook and the game script (request.txt, last_result.txt, reset.req, restore.req): never put it in a manifest, ignore it in every tree check, and never delete it (a pending reset.req / restore.req or an unread last_result.txt may be waiting there). Pinned (index, address and every code byte identical): KR_T9HomeCasual, KR_T9HomeConfig, C_SceneHomebase@CheckGameSysButtons, C_SceneHomebase@Run, LSys3xScript::RunEvent, KR_T18RunSandboxed. r15's nine, r18's one and r20's seven same-length sites and r19's five / r18's eight forwarders stay. Every earlier contract stays in force.",
